  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Metadata Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `metadata.json` file. I\'ve updated the `name` field to \"NovaPath\" and populated the `description` with a concise overview: \"Personal Opportunity Execution Agent transforming student career goals into personalized multi-step action plans with persistent memory.\" I\'m ensuring everything is formatted correctly and accurately represents the project\'s core purpose.\n\n\n**Analyzing Tool Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating external search tools and skill gap analyses. I\'m exploring an `OpportunitySearchTool` abstraction, making sure it can handle live queries and offer fallback datasets. Each opportunity will have detailed metadata including title, organization, and type, with clear tags for source transparency, ensuring it aligns with multi-step reasoning.\n\n\n**Defining Data Storage**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining persistent user memory. I\'m building out detailed schemas for profile and interaction memory, covering degree, location, interests, preferences. This will be crucial for the demo flow, handling user-specified preferences across sessions. I\'m focusing on an interactive panel for memory management, letting users view, edit, and filter data items. Lastly, I\'m working to solidify database schema requirements for persistence.\n\n\n**Establishing Database Schemas**\n\nI\'ve finalized database table schemas, including `users`, `memories`, `opportunities`, `applications`, `saved_opportunities`, `agent_runs`, and `agent_steps`. Now, I\'m integrating this into a robust backend, focusing on SQLite or PostgreSQL compatibility with schema migrations and Supabase export. I\'m also now focusing on match scoring and skill gap analysis, and the specifics of the 5-factor scoring model. I will be sure to display detailed score breakdowns.\n\n\n**Developing Full-Stack APIs**\n\nI\'m now building out the full stack, including an Express server and comprehensive REST APIs. I\'m focusing on GET and PUT methods for profile and memory, POST and DELETE for memory, and the core `POST /api/agent/run` endpoint for orchestrated agent execution. There\'s also API endpoints for opportunity and application management, plus a demo reset endpoint. The Gemini 3.7 Flash server-side integration is underway, leveraging `@google/genai` to enable robust reasoning. I\'m making a migration guide and schema.sql file.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 929626152
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
