  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Backend Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the backend architecture, specifically the database schema. I\'ve started outlining the tables, including `users`, `memories`, `opportunities`, `applications`, `agent_runs`, and `agent_steps`. I plan to integrate Supabase/PostgreSQL best practices for a robust and scalable structure.\n\n\n**Refining Database Details**\n\nI\'m now refining the database details, focusing on indexes and RLS policies to enhance performance and security. I\'ve been working on `database/store.ts` that will act as a persistent relational database engine, storing tables in JSON storage, that uses CRUD operations with relational queries and auto-initialization. I\'m building it with seed reset capabilities, and Supabase client adapter readiness.\n\n\n**Outlining Agent Workflow**\n\nMy focus has shifted to outlining the agent\'s workflow, breaking it into distinct steps. I\'ve designed a 10-step process, starting with goal decomposition and progressing through opportunity search, fit evaluation, and skill gap analysis. Each agent step is meticulously recorded in the database for comprehensive execution visibility and inspectability.\n\n\n**Mapping API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m mapping out the API endpoints. I\'m focusing on user-specific memory retrieval with `GET /api/memory/:userId` and CRUD operations for memories. I\'ve also incorporated endpoints for agent runs, history retrieval, managing opportunities, and applications. There is a demo endpoint for session set-up too.\n\n**Structuring Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m structuring the frontend components. I\'ve defined all the types in `src/types.ts`. I\'m building `src/services/api.ts` to manage the client-side API. The navigation is in `src/components/Navigation.tsx`, which has tabs, and I\'ve started building components like `GoalInput.tsx`, `AgentExecutionPanel.tsx`, and `OpportunityCard`.\n\n\n**Building UI Components**\n\nI\'m deep in building specific UI components now. I\'m focused on a clean `OpportunityCard` with match percentage, skill breakdowns, and action buttons. The `SkillGapCard` visualizes skill comparisons and learning recommendations. I\'m also working on `ActionPlanView` for a structured timeline and a dynamic `MemoryPanel`. Plus, I\'m building a demo controller for the hackathon and the main `Dashboard` page. Finally, a `ProfilePage` for student data is next.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 676100643
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
