    thinking: "**Defining Frontend Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m defining the frontend architecture. I\'m focusing on key components like the API client (`src/services/api.ts`) for clean, typed connections to `/api/*`, and the Navbar (`src/components/Navbar.tsx`) as a foundational UI element. This structure should lay the groundwork well.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve been designing the UI components. I\'m focusing on the professional header, including the product logo, navigation tabs (Dashboard, Profile, Opportunities, Action Plan, Memory), and the Judge Demo Mode toolbar. Also, I\'m working on the `GoalInput.tsx` for prompt input with one-click quick scenarios. Plus, the Agent Execution Panel.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Features**\n\nNow I\'m detailing specific project features. I\'m prioritizing the `PlanView.tsx` component with its categorized timeline and completion tracking. Also, I\'m working on the `MemoryPanel.tsx`, which will display Profile Memory and Interaction Memory. I am also working on `DemoController.tsx` for hackathon judges with demo phases and state reset. Finally, I\'m integrating these components into the dashboard.\n\nI am also defining the `ProfilePage.tsx` for editing student details, and the `OpportunitiesPage.tsx` with saved and applied opportunities. I also started working on the `PlanPage.tsx`. And of course, the `MemoryPage.tsx`.\n\n\n"
