  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///README.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "# NovaPath \342\200\224 Your Personal Opportunity Execution Agent\n\n> **LaunchPadX 2026 \342\200\224 Track 01: The Agent Hub**  \n> Built by **NovaForge** (5-member student engineering team)  \n> *Transforming student career goals into personalized, multi-step execution plans using persistent memory and external opportunity tools.*\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Overview\n\n**NovaPath** is a student-first AI opportunity execution agent designed for engineering undergraduates. Rather than acting as a standard conversational chatbot or a passive job search aggregator, NovaPath decomposes a student\'s high-level career goal into structured subtasks, retrieves long-term profile and interaction memory, interacts with external and curated opportunity data sources, computes transparent 5-factor fit scores, identifies concrete skill gaps, and generates an executable timeline action plan.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Problem Statement\n\n1. **Information Overload & Passive Job Boards**: Students are bombarded with hundreds of job listings across fragmented portals with zero personalized guidance on eligibility or fit.\n2. **Stateless AI Chatbots**: Generic conversational LLMs lack persistent memory across sessions, require students to repeatedly paste resumes and preferences, and often hallucinate non-existent jobs or unrealistic guarantees.\n3. **Missing Execution Guidance**: Finding an opportunity is only 20% of the battle; knowing which technical skill gaps to bridge, what mini-projects to build, and what daily actions to take before deadlines is what drives actual success.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The Solution: NovaPath\n\nNovaPath introduces an **agentic execution loop**:\n\n```\nSTUDENT GOAL\n     \342\206\223\nAGENT ORCHESTRATOR (10 Decomposed Subtasks)\n     \342\206\223\nPERSISTENT MEMORY & STUDENT PROFILE\n     \342\206\223\nEXTERNAL OPPORTUNITY SEARCH TOOL\n     \342\206\223\n5-FACTOR DETERMINISTIC MATCH EVALUATION\n     \342\206\223\nSKILL-GAP & ROADMAP ANALYSIS\n     \342\206\223\nCONCRETE ACTION PLAN (Today / 3 Days / This Week / 2 Weeks)\n     \342\206\223\nLONG-TERM PREFERENCE PERSISTENCE\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Features & Track 01 Requirements\n\n### Requirement A: Multi-Step Reasoning & Task Decomposition\n* **10-Step Visible Execution Stepper**:\n  1. `understand_objective`: Decomposes natural language intent, role, and constraints.\n  2. `load_profile`: Fetches student\'s verified degree, branch, year, and skills.\n  3. `retrieve_memory`: Recalls long-term preferences, past interactions, and location choices.\n  4. `plan_search`: Formulates targeted search criteria.\n  5. `search_opportunities`: Queries external/curated opportunity tools.\n  6. `evaluate_fit`: Runs transparent 5-factor scoring algorithm.\n  7. `identify_skill_gaps`: Calculates missing skills vs. candidate pool requirements.\n  8. `rank_opportunities`: Sorts and highlights top matches.\n  9. `generate_action_plan`: Builds structured, timeline-based execution checklist.\n  10. `update_memory`: Persists newly identified preferences to long-term memory.\n\n### Requirement B: External Tool / API Interaction (`OpportunitySearchTool`)\n* Standardized `OpportunitySearchTool` abstraction with query filtering across domain, location, remote preference, and eligibility.\n* Source provenance badges: **LIVE VERIFIED**, **CACHED**, or **CURATED DATASET**.\n* Real organizations, deadlines, stipends, and verifiable official portal URLs.\n\n### Requirement C: Persistent User Memory\n* **Profile Memory**: Stable academic background (e.g., B.Tech 2nd Year, AI/ML, Hyderabad).\n* **Interaction & Preference Memory**: Dynamic knowledge retained across sessions.\n* **Demonstrable 2-Session Workflow**:\n  * **Session 1**: User states *\"I prefer Hyderabad and remote internships.\"* \342\206\222 Saved to memory.\n  * **Session 2**: User enters *\"Find opportunities for me.\"* \342\206\222 NovaPath automatically recalls preferences and searches without requiring manual input.\n\n### Requirement D: Relational Database & Supabase Readiness\n* Full Supabase / PostgreSQL schema included in `database/supabase_schema.sql`.\n* Logical tables: `users`, `memories`, `opportunities`, `applications`, `agent_runs`, `agent_steps`.\n* Zero external native dependencies needed for development in containerized environments.\n\n### Requirement E: Deterministic 5-Factor Match Scoring\n* **Skills Match**: 40%\n* **Eligibility Match**: 25%\n* **Location Preference**: 15%\n* **Opportunity Type Preference**: 10%\n* **Experience & Year Fit**: 10%\n\n---\n\n## 5. System Architecture\n\n```\nnovapath/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.tsx             # Main header & section navigation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DemoController.tsx     # Hackathon Judge 1-click test suite\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 GoalInput.tsx          # Goal prompt input with suggestions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AgentExecutionPanel.tsx# Live 10-step execution stepper\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 OpportunityCard.tsx    # Card with 5-factor score breakdown\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SkillGapCard.tsx       # Skill bridge & hands-on mini projects\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ActionPlanView.tsx     # Checklist timeline\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 MemoryPanel.tsx        # Persistent memory manager\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Dashboard.tsx          # Main command center\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfilePage.tsx        # Student academic profile editor\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 OpportunitiesPage.tsx  # Application tracker\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PlanPage.tsx           # Full execution roadmap\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 MemoryPage.tsx         # Memory audit log\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 api.ts                 # Typed client API layer\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types.ts                   # Core TypeScript domain models\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                    # Root application component\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx                   # React 19 entry point\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 agent/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 orchestrator.ts            # 10-step agent reasoning pipeline\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tools/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 opportunity_search.ts      # OpportunitySearchTool abstraction\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 gemini.ts                  # Server-side Gemini 3.7 Flash integration\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 scoring.ts                 # 5-factor deterministic evaluation\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 store.ts                   # Relational database engine & seed data\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 supabase_schema.sql        # Supabase/PostgreSQL migration DDL\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                      # Express API server + Vite middleware\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Setup Instructions\n\n### Prerequisites\n* Node.js 18+ or 20+\n* npm, pnpm, or bun\n\n### 1. Install Dependencies\n```bash\nnpm install\n```\n\n### 2. Configure Environment Variables\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env`:\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n```\n\nSet your Gemini API key (optional for fallback mode, required for live LLM reasoning):\n```env\nGEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here\n```\n\n### 3. Start Development Server\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\nThe application will be accessible at `http://localhost:3000`.\n\n### 4. Production Build\n```bash\nnpm run build\nnpm run start\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. API Endpoints\n\n| Method | Endpoint | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET` | `/api/health` | Service health status |\n| `GET` | `/api/profile/:id` | Retrieve student profile |\n| `PUT` | `/api/profile/:id` | Update student profile |\n| `GET` | `/api/memory/:userId` | List persistent memories |\n| `POST` | `/api/memory` | Store new memory preference |\n| `DELETE` | `/api/memory/:id` | Delete memory node |\n| `POST` | `/api/agent/run` | Execute multi-step agent workflow |\n| `GET` | `/api/agent/run/:id` | Inspect execution run & subtask steps |\n| `GET` | `/api/opportunities` | Get verified opportunities |\n| `GET` | `/api/applications/:userId` | Get saved & tracked applications |\n| `POST` | `/api/applications` | Save or update application stage |\n| `POST` | `/api/demo/preset` | Trigger Hackathon judge demo preset |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Hackathon Judge Demo Walkthrough\n\n### Scenario 1: First Session (Specify Preferences)\n1. In the top **LaunchPadX 2026 Judge Quick-Demo** banner, click **`Session 1: \"AI/ML in Hyderabad\"`**.\n2. Observe the **10-Step Execution Panel** step-by-step progress.\n3. Review the ranked opportunities, match breakdown (e.g. CognitiveScale, Microsoft R&D, Swiggy Tech Labs), identified skill gaps (TensorFlow, Docker), and the action plan.\n4. Note that NovaPath saves the preference for *Hyderabad* and *AI/ML* to memory.\n\n### Scenario 2: Second Session (Memory Recall)\n1. Click **`Session 2: \"Find for me\" (Memory Recall)`**.\n2. Goal is simply: *\"Find opportunities for me.\"*\n3. Notice how the agent automatically retrieves:\n   * `\342\234\223 Target location: Hyderabad`\n   * `\342\234\223 Remote flexibility preferred`\n   * `\342\234\223 Student: Rahul (B.Tech Year 2)`\n4. The agent executes and returns tailored opportunities without requiring the user to re-enter anything!\n\n---\n\n## 9. Future Roadmap\n\n* **Phase 2**: Resume PDF parsing and GitHub portfolio analyzer.\n* **Phase 3**: Google Calendar interview synchronization and email reminders.\n* **Phase 4**: College placement cell institutional analytics dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## 10. License & Credits\n\nDeveloped with \342\235\244\357\270\217 by **NovaForge** for LaunchPadX 2026.\n"
    }
    diff {
      unified_diff {
