  planner_response {
    response: "You can inspect and manage your database and dashboard in two primary ways:\n\n---\n\n### 1. In the Live Web Application (Interactive Agent & Memory Dashboard)\nInside the app preview interface:\n\n* **Executive Dashboard (`Dashboard` tab)**: View real-time career trajectory insights, active agent executions, opportunity match rankings, and live trending tech stacks.\n* **Agent Nova Hub (`Agent Nova` / `Chat` tab)**: Test multi-step autonomous planning, tool calls, and intent decomposition with live feedback.\n* **Persistent Memory Bank (`Memory` tab)**: Directly view, inspect, and delete long-term student memories, preferences, and verified skill signals stored in the database.\n* **Student Profile (`Profile` tab)**: Update your academic background, skills, degree, target domains, and verified credentials.\n\n---\n\n### 2. In the Google Cloud / Firebase Console (Raw Cloud Firestore Data)\nYour project\'s Firestore database is:\n**`ai-studio-novapath-5ca8369d-858f-48b8-8666-37a99a9dd53d`**\n\nTo watch the live documents, subcollections, and security rules:\n\n1. Go to the [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/) or [Google Cloud Firestore Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/firestore).\n2. Select your project.\n3. Open **Firestore Database** in the left navigation sidebar.\n4. You will see the structured collections:\n   * **`users/{userId}/profile/data`**: Student academic backgrounds, target domains, and verified skills.\n   * **`users/{userId}/memories/{memoryId}`**: Real-time cross-session agent memory bank (semantic memory items, preferences, and verified badges).\n   * **`users/{userId}/agentRuns/{runId}`**: Full multi-step agent reasoning traces, decomposed subtasks, and transparency reports.\n   * **`users/{userId}/savedOpportunities/{opportunityId}`**: Tracked internships, hackathons, and application pipeline statuses.\n   * **`opportunities/{opportunityId}`**: Opportunity catalog used by the transparent matching engine.\n5. In the **Rules** tab, you can also view and audit the active `firestore.rules`."
    modified_response: "You can inspect and manage your database and dashboard in two primary ways:\n\n---\n\n### 1. In the Live Web Application (Interactive Agent & Memory Dashboard)\nInside the app preview interface:\n\n* **Executive Dashboard (`Dashboard` tab)**: View real-time career trajectory insights, active agent executions, opportunity match rankings, and live trending tech stacks.\n* **Agent Nova Hub (`Agent Nova` / `Chat` tab)**: Test multi-step autonomous planning, tool calls, and intent decomposition with live feedback.\n* **Persistent Memory Bank (`Memory` tab)**: Directly view, inspect, and delete long-term student memories, preferences, and verified skill signals stored in the database.\n* **Student Profile (`Profile` tab)**: Update your academic background, skills, degree, target domains, and verified credentials.\n\n---\n\n### 2. In the Google Cloud / Firebase Console (Raw Cloud Firestore Data)\nYour project\'s Firestore database is:\n**`ai-studio-novapath-5ca8369d-858f-48b8-8666-37a99a9dd53d`**\n\nTo watch the live documents, subcollections, and security rules:\n\n1. Go to the [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/) or [Google Cloud Firestore Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/firestore).\n2. Select your project.\n3. Open **Firestore Database** in the left navigation sidebar.\n4. You will see the structured collections:\n   * **`users/{userId}/profile/data`**: Student academic backgrounds, target domains, and verified skills.\n   * **`users/{userId}/memories/{memoryId}`**: Real-time cross-session agent memory bank (semantic memory items, preferences, and verified badges).\n   * **`users/{userId}/agentRuns/{runId}`**: Full multi-step agent reasoning traces, decomposed subtasks, and transparency reports.\n   * **`users/{userId}/savedOpportunities/{opportunityId}`**: Tracked internships, hackathons, and application pipeline statuses.\n   * **`opportunities/{opportunityId}`**: Opportunity catalog used by the transparent matching engine.\n5. In the **Rules** tab, you can also view and audit the active `firestore.rules`."
