  planner_response {
    response: "Yes, the application utilizes the following API keys and credentials:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Google Gemini API Key (`GEMINI_API_KEY`)**\n* **Usage**: Powers **Agent Nova**\'s multi-step autonomous planning, natural language career intent decomposition, dynamic opportunity gap diagnosis, and live conversational chat.\n* **Security & Architecture**: \n  - Kept strictly **server-side** inside the backend Express service (`server.ts` & `agent/orchestrator.ts`).\n  - It is **never exposed** to the client browser or frontend bundle.\n  - Injected automatically by the AI Studio environment via `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n  - Includes a fallback heuristic intelligence engine if the key is not present or rate-limited.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Firebase Public Web Configuration Key (`apiKey`)**\n* **Usage**: Connects the client app to **Firebase Authentication** and **Cloud Firestore Database** (`src/firebase/config.ts`).\n* **Security & Architecture**: \n  - Standard Firebase public client identifier used to identify your project (`gen-lang-client-0478358580`) on Google\'s edge endpoints.\n  - Access to data is securely enforced via **Cloud Firestore Security Rules** (`firestore.rules`), ensuring users can only read and write their own student records and memories.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Key / Credential | Environment Variable / Location | Scope | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Gemini API Key** | `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` | Server-Side Only (Private) | Agent Nova reasoning, intent decomposition & AI chat |\n| **Firebase Web Config** | `src/firebase/config.ts` | Client-Side (Public Identifier) | Firestore real-time DB & User Authentication |"
