  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the architectural and configuration inspection of the Gemini integration in NovaPath:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where `GEMINI_API_KEY` is Configured\n- **Environment Definition**: Declared in `.env.example` as `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n- **Runtime Access**: Accessed strictly via Node.js environment variables (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`) on the server.\n- **Client Instantiation**: Lazily initialized in `/services/gemini.ts` using the `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK:\n  ```typescript\n  new GoogleGenAI({\n    apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY,\n    httpOptions: { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\' } }\n  })\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Secret Type: AI Studio-Managed vs. Manually Configured\n- **AI Studio-Managed Secret**: In the Google AI Studio environment, `GEMINI_API_KEY` is injected automatically by the platform into the server runtime container.\n- For local/external execution outside AI Studio, it can optionally be supplied via a standard environment variable or `.env` file as documented in `README.md`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Google Cloud Project Associated with Gemini API Calls\n- The Gemini API calls execute within the **Google Cloud project hosting the AI Studio instance** (`gen-lang-client-0478358580` / Project Number: `1036154777635`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Gemini API & Models Currently in Use\n- **SDK**: Official `@google/genai` (Google Gen AI SDK for Node.js).\n- **Models Used**:\n  - **Primary**: `gemini-3.7-flash` (used for agent intent decomposition, Google Search grounding, live trends discovery, and career mentorship chat).\n  - **Fallback / Low-Latency Tier**: `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` (used for fast fallbacks and lightweight tasks).\n  - **Deterministic Heuristic Engine**: Built-in algorithmic fallback if the API is unreachable or rate-limited.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Server-Side Files that Access `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n1. **/services/gemini.ts**: The central integration layer that directly reads `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`, instantiates `GoogleGenAI`, and runs prompt executions (`chatWithAgentNova`, `parseGoalWithAI`, `searchWebOpportunities`, `fetchDailyTechTrends`).\n2. **/agent/orchestrator.ts**: Consumes the Gemini service during Step 1 of the 10-step agent reasoning loop (Intent & Goal decomposition).\n3. **/server.ts**: Exposes Express REST endpoints (`/api/agent/chat`, `/api/agent/trends`, `/api/agent/search`) that invoke the Gemini services server-side.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Client-Side Bundle Security Confirmation\n- **Confirmed: `GEMINI_API_KEY` can NEVER be included in the client-side JavaScript bundle.**\n- The key does **not** use the `VITE_` prefix (which Vite requires to expose variables to browser code).\n- All Gemini API calls run inside the Express Node.js backend (`server.ts` / `services/gemini.ts`), and the browser communicates exclusively with `/api/*` backend routes.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Reusability for the ATS (Applicant Tracking System) Feature\n- **Yes, the current Gemini integration can be directly reused for ATS.**\n- The existing `/services/gemini.ts` module can be extended with dedicated helper functions (e.g., `analyzeResumeATS()`, `calculateKeywordMatch()`, `generateResumeOptimizationTips()`) leveraging the already initialized `getGeminiClient()` and `gemini-3.7-flash` model.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Need for an Additional Gemini API Key for ATS\n- **No, you do NOT need to provide another API key.**\n- The existing server-side `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `@google/genai` client instance will handle ATS resume parsing, scoring, and feedback seamlessly without any extra credentials."
    modified_response: "Here is the architectural and configuration inspection of the Gemini integration in NovaPath:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where `GEMINI_API_KEY` is Configured\n- **Environment Definition**: Declared in `.env.example` as `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n- **Runtime Access**: Accessed strictly via Node.js environment variables (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`) on the server.\n- **Client Instantiation**: Lazily initialized in `/services/gemini.ts` using the `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK:\n  ```typescript\n  new GoogleGenAI({\n    apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY,\n    httpOptions: { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\' } }\n  })\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Secret Type: AI Studio-Managed vs. Manually Configured\n- **AI Studio-Managed Secret**: In the Google AI Studio environment, `GEMINI_API_KEY` is injected automatically by the platform into the server runtime container.\n- For local/external execution outside AI Studio, it can optionally be supplied via a standard environment variable or `.env` file as documented in `README.md`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Google Cloud Project Associated with Gemini API Calls\n- The Gemini API calls execute within the **Google Cloud project hosting the AI Studio instance** (`gen-lang-client-0478358580` / Project Number: `1036154777635`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Gemini API & Models Currently in Use\n- **SDK**: Official `@google/genai` (Google Gen AI SDK for Node.js).\n- **Models Used**:\n  - **Primary**: `gemini-3.7-flash` (used for agent intent decomposition, Google Search grounding, live trends discovery, and career mentorship chat).\n  - **Fallback / Low-Latency Tier**: `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` (used for fast fallbacks and lightweight tasks).\n  - **Deterministic Heuristic Engine**: Built-in algorithmic fallback if the API is unreachable or rate-limited.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Server-Side Files that Access `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n1. **/services/gemini.ts**: The central integration layer that directly reads `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`, instantiates `GoogleGenAI`, and runs prompt executions (`chatWithAgentNova`, `parseGoalWithAI`, `searchWebOpportunities`, `fetchDailyTechTrends`).\n2. **/agent/orchestrator.ts**: Consumes the Gemini service during Step 1 of the 10-step agent reasoning loop (Intent & Goal decomposition).\n3. **/server.ts**: Exposes Express REST endpoints (`/api/agent/chat`, `/api/agent/trends`, `/api/agent/search`) that invoke the Gemini services server-side.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Client-Side Bundle Security Confirmation\n- **Confirmed: `GEMINI_API_KEY` can NEVER be included in the client-side JavaScript bundle.**\n- The key does **not** use the `VITE_` prefix (which Vite requires to expose variables to browser code).\n- All Gemini API calls run inside the Express Node.js backend (`server.ts` / `services/gemini.ts`), and the browser communicates exclusively with `/api/*` backend routes.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Reusability for the ATS (Applicant Tracking System) Feature\n- **Yes, the current Gemini integration can be directly reused for ATS.**\n- The existing `/services/gemini.ts` module can be extended with dedicated helper functions (e.g., `analyzeResumeATS()`, `calculateKeywordMatch()`, `generateResumeOptimizationTips()`) leveraging the already initialized `getGeminiClient()` and `gemini-3.7-flash` model.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Need for an Additional Gemini API Key for ATS\n- **No, you do NOT need to provide another API key.**\n- The existing server-side `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `@google/genai` client instance will handle ATS resume parsing, scoring, and feedback seamlessly without any extra credentials."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
