  user_input {
    user_response: "Now implement the ATS Resume Scanner in the existing NovaPath application.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe existing Gemini integration has already been verified.\n\nReuse:\n- /services/gemini.ts\n- getGeminiClient()\n- existing GEMINI_API_KEY\n- existing Express backend\n- existing Firebase configuration\n- existing Firebase Authentication\n\nDO NOT:\n- Create another Gemini API key\n- Create another Gemini client\n- Create a second Gemini service\n- Expose GEMINI_API_KEY to the frontend\n- Put GEMINI_API_KEY in Firestore\n- Put GEMINI_API_KEY in localStorage/sessionStorage\n- Put GEMINI_API_KEY in client-side code\n- Break existing Agent Nova functionality\n\n==================================================\n1. ATS FEATURE\n==================================================\n\nAdd a new navigation section:\n\nATS Scanner\n\nThe existing NovaPath UI and design system must be preserved.\n\nThe ATS feature should allow a user to:\n\n1. Upload a resume\n2. Optionally provide a job description\n3. Analyze the resume\n4. Receive an ATS Readiness Score\n5. See detected problems\n6. See matched keywords\n7. See missing relevant keywords\n8. See formatting/parsing risks\n9. Receive actionable recommendations\n10. Receive improved bullet suggestions\n11. Save the report\n12. Reopen previous reports\n\n==================================================\n2. SUPPORTED FILES\n==================================================\n\nSupport:\n\n- PDF\n- DOCX\n- PNG\n- JPG\n- JPEG\n\nValidate:\n\n- File type\n- File size\n- Empty files\n- Corrupted files\n\nUse a reasonable maximum file size.\n\nShow:\n\n- File name\n- File size\n- Upload progress\n- Processing status\n- Remove/replace option\n\n==================================================\n3. FIREBASE STORAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse Firebase Storage for uploaded resumes.\n\nUse a structure similar to:\n\nresumes/{userId}/{resumeId}/{fileName}\n\nEach upload must have a unique resumeId.\n\nDo NOT store resume binary data in Firestore.\n\nStore only metadata in Firestore.\n\nExample:\n\nusers/{userId}/resumes/{resumeId}\n\n{\n  resumeId,\n  fileName,\n  fileType,\n  storagePath,\n  uploadedAt,\n  status\n}\n\nFiles must not be public.\n\nOnly the authenticated owner may access their resume.\n\n==================================================\n4. FIRESTORE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nusers/{userId}/resumes/{resumeId}\n\nand:\n\nusers/{userId}/atsReports/{reportId}\n\nATS report example:\n\n{\n  reportId,\n  resumeId,\n  score,\n  jobTitle,\n  createdAt,\n  status,\n\n  categoryScores: {\n    keywordMatch,\n    structure,\n    experienceQuality,\n    skillsAlignment,\n    atsReadability,\n    contactInformation\n  },\n\n  matchedKeywords: [],\n  missingKeywords: [],\n  formattingIssues: [],\n  contentIssues: [],\n  recommendations: [],\n  bulletImprovements: []\n}\n\nUse Firestore timestamps.\n\n==================================================\n5. FIREBASE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nImplement secure Firestore rules.\n\nAuthenticated user UID must match the path UID.\n\nA user must only be able to access:\n\nusers/{theirOwnUid}/...\n\nDo not use:\n\nallow read, write: if true;\n\nImplement equivalent ownership protection for Firebase Storage.\n\nA user must not be able to access another user\'s:\n\n- Resume\n- Resume metadata\n- ATS reports\n\n==================================================\n6. GEMINI INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nExtend the existing:\n\n/services/gemini.ts\n\nDo not create a duplicate Gemini integration.\n\nAdd dedicated functions such as:\n\nanalyzeResumeATS()\nextractResumeData()\nanalyzeJobMatch()\ngenerateResumeRecommendations()\n\nReuse:\n\ngetGeminiClient()\n\nand the existing Gemini configuration.\n\nKeep Gemini calls server-side.\n\n==================================================\n7. RESUME EXTRACTION\n==================================================\n\nExtract:\n\n- Name\n- Email\n- Phone\n- LinkedIn\n- GitHub\n- Summary\n- Education\n- Experience\n- Projects\n- Skills\n- Certifications\n- Achievements\n\nReturn structured JSON.\n\nIf a field is not present:\n\nreturn null or [].\n\nNEVER invent information.\n\nIf the uploaded resume is an image:\n\nuse Gemini multimodal capabilities or the existing appropriate document/image processing mechanism.\n\n==================================================\n8. JOB DESCRIPTION\n==================================================\n\nAdd an optional input:\n\n\"Paste Job Description\"\n\nIf no job description is provided:\n\nPerform general ATS-readiness analysis.\n\nIf a job description is provided:\n\nCompare the resume against it.\n\nIdentify:\n\n- Matched skills\n- Missing relevant skills\n- Important keywords\n- Related terminology\n- Experience alignment\n- Education alignment\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo not tell users to claim skills they do not have.\n\nUse:\n\n\"Consider adding this skill if you have relevant experience.\"\n\nDo not encourage keyword stuffing.\n\n==================================================\n9. ATS ANALYSIS\n==================================================\n\nAnalyze:\n\nA. Contact information\nB. Resume structure\nC. Standard section headings\nD. Skills\nE. Keywords\nF. Experience\nG. Projects\nH. Formatting/parsing risks\nI. Job description alignment\n\nPotential parsing risks may include:\n\n- Complex tables\n- Multi-column layouts\n- Text embedded in images\n- Unusual section headings\n- Important information inside headers/footers\n- Excessive decorative elements\n- Inconsistent formatting\n\nDo NOT state that a particular formatting choice automatically fails every ATS.\n\nUse language such as:\n\n\"Potential parsing risk.\"\n\n==================================================\n10. DETERMINISTIC SCORING\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT let Gemini randomly decide the final score.\n\nCreate:\n\n/features/ats/services/atsScoringService.ts\n\nor follow the existing project architecture.\n\nCalculate:\n\nKeyword relevance: 25 points\nResume structure: 20 points\nExperience/content quality: 20 points\nSkills alignment: 15 points\nATS readability: 10 points\nContact information: 10 points\n\nTotal = 100.\n\nGemini provides structured findings.\n\nThe application calculates the final score.\n\nDisplay:\n\nATS Readiness Score: XX/100\n\nAlso display category scores.\n\n==================================================\n11. ISSUE PRIORITY\n==================================================\n\nEvery issue must contain:\n\n- severity\n- category\n- problem\n- whyItMatters\n- recommendation\n\nSeverity:\n\nHIGH\nMEDIUM\nLOW\n\nShow the most important 3\342\200\2235 issues first.\n\n==================================================\n12. BULLET IMPROVEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nAnalyze resume bullets.\n\nLook for:\n\n- Action verbs\n- Technical specificity\n- Clear responsibility\n- Results\n- Technologies\n- Conciseness\n\nGemini may rewrite bullets.\n\nBUT:\n\nThe rewritten version must only use facts already present in the resume.\n\nNEVER invent:\n\n- Numbers\n- Percentages\n- Users\n- Revenue\n- Technologies\n- Certifications\n- Awards\n- Companies\n- Achievements\n\nIf a measurable result is missing:\n\nsay:\n\n\"Consider adding a real measurable result if available.\"\n\n==================================================\n13. API DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing Express server.\n\nAdd appropriate backend routes, for example:\n\nPOST /api/ats/upload\nPOST /api/ats/analyze\nGET /api/ats/reports\nGET /api/ats/reports/:reportId\nDELETE /api/ats/reports/:reportId\n\nFollow the existing NovaPath API conventions.\n\nAll routes must verify authentication.\n\nDo not expose Gemini credentials.\n\n==================================================\n14. ANALYSIS FLOW\n==================================================\n\nImplement:\n\nUpload:\n\nFrontend\n \342\206\223\nPOST /api/ats/upload\n \342\206\223\nAuthenticated backend\n \342\206\223\nFirebase Storage\n \342\206\223\nFirestore resume metadata\n\nAnalysis:\n\nFrontend\n \342\206\223\nPOST /api/ats/analyze\n \342\206\223\nBackend retrieves/reads resume\n \342\206\223\nExisting Gemini service\n \342\206\223\nStructured resume analysis\n \342\206\223\nKeyword analysis\n \342\206\223\nJob description analysis\n \342\206\223\nDeterministic ATS scoring\n \342\206\223\nFirestore ATS report\n \342\206\223\nFrontend results\n\n==================================================\n15. PROCESSING UI\n==================================================\n\nShow meaningful progress states:\n\nUploading resume...\n\342\234\223 Resume uploaded\n\nReading resume...\n\342\234\223 Resume content extracted\n\nAnalyzing resume structure...\n\342\234\223 Structure analyzed\n\nChecking keywords...\n\342\234\223 Keywords analyzed\n\nComparing with job description...\n\342\234\223 Job match analyzed\n\nCalculating ATS readiness...\n\342\234\223 Score calculated\n\nGenerating recommendations...\n\342\234\223 Recommendations ready\n\nDo not use only a generic spinner.\n\n==================================================\n16. RESULTS UI\n==================================================\n\nDisplay:\n\nATS Readiness Score\n\nCategory Scores\n\nHigh Priority Issues\n\nMedium Priority Issues\n\nLow Priority Issues\n\nMatched Keywords\n\nMissing Relevant Keywords\n\nFormatting Risks\n\nContent Issues\n\nRecommended Changes\n\nImproved Bullet Suggestions\n\nIf a job description was provided:\n\nJob Match Score\n\nKeep the UI clean and easy to understand.\n\n==================================================\n17. REPORT HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nAdd:\n\nPrevious ATS Reports\n\nDisplay:\n\n- Resume name\n- Score\n- Job title\n- Date\n- Status\n\nAllow:\n\nOpen Report\nDelete Report\n\nOnly show reports belonging to the authenticated user.\n\n==================================================\n18. DELETE\n==================================================\n\nWhen deleting a resume/report:\n\nDelete associated Firestore metadata.\n\nDelete associated Firebase Storage file when appropriate.\n\nHandle failures safely.\n\n==================================================\n19. PRIVACY\n==================================================\n\nDo not log complete resume contents.\n\nDo not expose resume data publicly.\n\nDo not unnecessarily store duplicate copies.\n\nAdd a privacy message:\n\n\"Your resume is processed to generate your ATS analysis and stored securely in your NovaPath account.\"\n\n==================================================\n20. ERROR HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nHandle:\n\n- Not authenticated\n- Invalid file\n- File too large\n- Upload failure\n- Storage failure\n- Resume extraction failure\n- Gemini failure\n- Invalid Gemini response\n- Firestore failure\n- Network failure\n- Empty resume\n\nNever crash the entire NovaPath application.\n\n==================================================\n21. BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementation, verify that the existing features still work:\n\n- Login\n- Dashboard\n- Agent Nova\n- Gemini chat\n- Agent reasoning\n- Search\n- Trends\n- Existing profile\n- Existing memory\n- Existing Firebase functionality\n\nDo not modify unrelated files unless necessary.\n\n==================================================\n22. SECURITY CHECK\n==================================================\n\nBefore finishing, verify:\n\n1. GEMINI_API_KEY is only accessed through process.env on the server.\n2. No GEMINI_API_KEY exists in frontend code.\n3. No Gemini secret is returned by an API response.\n4. Firebase Storage is authenticated.\n5. Firestore is authenticated.\n6. User A cannot access User B\'s reports.\n7. User A cannot access User B\'s resume.\n8. Resume files are not publicly accessible.\n9. API routes validate authentication.\n\n==================================================\n23. FINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementation, give me:\n\n1. Files created\n2. Files modified\n3. Firebase Storage changes\n4. Firestore changes\n5. Security rules changes\n6. Gemini service changes\n7. API routes added\n8. Dependencies added\n9. Environment variables required\n10. Tests performed\n11. Known limitations\n12. Any Firebase Console configuration I still need to perform manually\n\nDo not print any secret values."
