  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements Carefully**\n\nI\'m deep in the requirements analysis, meticulously examining each feature. The current focus is on the \"ATS Scanner\" tab and its navigation. I\'m considering Lucide icons like `FileCheck` or `Search` to represent it. I must ensure the UI is intuitive and easy to use. I\'m planning to move on to backend architecture shortly.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI for the ATS scanner, particularly the resume upload and progress visualization. I\'ve decided on the design, considering Lucide icons like `ScanLine` or `FileText`. I plan to mirror NovaPath\'s existing UI to maintain a consistent look. I\'ve designed the progress states, from resume upload to score calculation. I\'m also planning the results UI; I\'m planning to use a radial gauge for the ATS readiness score and also partitioning issues by priority. I\'ve prepared a privacy note.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been working on the data structures. I\'ve defined the structure for ATS reports, including detailed scoring, extracted resume data, issues, and recommendations. The Firestore rules are also updated for secure storage and data access. I also have the schema and the storage path, the basic backend is almost complete.\n\n\n**Establishing Backend Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on the backend logic, particularly the API routes. I\'m designing endpoints for resume uploads and data extraction using Multer, supporting various formats like PDF, DOCX, PNG, and JPG. I\'m planning to handle different resume data formats using a `ResumeData` object, and implementing functions to analyze resumes, job matches, and generate recommendations. I\'m going to integrate multimodal Gemini 3.7 Flash for images and use libraries like `pdf-parse` and `mammoth` for document parsing. I have also decided on safe prompt constraints. I\'m also planning deterministic scoring logic.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 436654570
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
