  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing a Role Blueprint**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on crafting a strategic blueprint for role selection, and it\'s evolving into a comprehensive plan. I\'m taking the user\'s request for modifications based on an ATS scan, and integrating that into a broader framework. This means the blueprint will incorporate resume optimization as a critical step, which is an exciting new component to be added.\n\n\n**Defining Role Adjustments**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the specifics for role adjustments identified via the ATS scan. I\'ve designed a structured approach, starting with a target profile for the role. This profile will include the role name, seniority level, and a probability assessment, and then, most crucially, a \'Tailored Modifications & Action Plan\'. This plan includes headline rewrites, project re-framing suggestions, and key technical skills recommendations.\n\n\n**Refining Actionable Blueprint**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into creating the actionable components of the blueprint. I\'m focusing on specific modifications for experience sections, shifting verbs, and adding new responsibilities. I\'m also including interview prep, architecture patterns and talking points aligned with the role, which makes it feel so much more complete. Finally, I\'ve created an application checklist of concrete steps before submitting the application. I\'ve designed a `RoleModificationBlueprint` data schema, which will guide the generation.\n\n\n**Implementing Role Integration**\n\nI\'m making progress by adding a `roleModifications` field to the `AtsReport` type and integrating Gemini to generate a tailored blueprint. This involves prompting Gemini to analyze the resume against the target role and then produce a detailed `roleModifications` object. Also, I\'m thinking of creating an interactive \"Role Selection Blueprint\" tab for a guided application.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 322004034
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
