steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787444375
      nanos: 505913319
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "I want to add a new major feature to my existing NovaPath application called:\n\nPERSONALIZED CAREER PATH\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is an EXISTING application.\n\nDo NOT rebuild the application from scratch.\n\nDo NOT replace the current UI design.\n\nDo NOT remove or break any existing functionality.\n\nPreserve all existing features, including:\n\n- Agent Hub\n- Agent Nova\n- AI Coach\n- ATS Scanner\n- Profile & Skills\n- Opportunities\n- Memory Bank\n- Firebase Authentication\n- Firebase Firestore\n- Firebase Storage\n- Existing Gemini integration\n- Existing server-side Express architecture\n- Existing API routes\n- Existing navigation and design system\n\nFirst inspect the existing codebase and understand how these features are currently implemented.\n\nThen implement the Career Path feature using the existing architecture and reusable components wherever possible.\n\n==================================================\nPRODUCT PURPOSE\n==================================================\n\nNovaPath is an AI career execution platform for students.\n\nThe new Career Path feature should answer:\n\n\"If I want to get this particular job, but I am not currently qualified, what exactly should I learn, build, and improve to become ready for that role?\"\n\nThe feature must NOT simply generate a generic career roadmap.\n\nIt must create a PERSONALIZED career path based on:\n\n- Student profile\n- Current skills\n- Education\n- Projects\n- Experience\n- Certifications\n- Target job\n- Target job requirements\n- Existing ATS analysis when available\n- Previously completed learning milestones\n- User preferences stored in memory when relevant\n\n==================================================\nCORE USER FLOW\n==================================================\n\nImplement this flow:\n\nStudent\n \342\206\223\nSelect Target Career / Job\n \342\206\223\nLoad Student Profile\n \342\206\223\nAnalyze Target Role Requirements\n \342\206\223\nCompare Student Skills vs Requirements\n \342\206\223\nIdentify Skill Gaps\n \342\206\223\nPrioritize Skill Gaps\n \342\206\223\nGenerate Personalized Career Path\n \342\206\223\nRecommend Verified Learning Resources\n \342\206\223\nRecommend Practical Projects\n \342\206\223\nCreate Timeline\n \342\206\223\nTrack Progress\n \342\206\223\nRecalculate Career Readiness\n \342\206\223\nRecommend When To Apply\n\n==================================================\n1. NEW NAVIGATION SECTION\n==================================================\n\nAdd:\n\nCareer Path\n\nto the existing navigation.\n\nUse the existing NovaPath visual language.\n\nDo not redesign the entire navbar.\n\nThe new page should feel like a native part of NovaPath.\n\nSuggested page title:\n\n\"Personalized Career Path\"\n\nSubtitle:\n\n\"Your step-by-step path from where you are today to the role you want.\"\n\n==================================================\n2. CAREER TARGET SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nAllow the student to select or enter a target role.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Machine Learning Engineer\n- Data Scientist\n- AI Engineer\n- Data Analyst\n- Full Stack Developer\n- Backend Developer\n- Software Engineer\n- Cloud Engineer\n\nAlso allow:\n\n\"Use an opportunity from Opportunities\"\n\nIf the user selects an actual job opportunity, use that opportunity\'s requirements instead of generating generic requirements.\n\n==================================================\n3. STUDENT PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nRetrieve the authenticated user\'s existing profile.\n\nUse available information such as:\n\n- Name\n- Degree\n- Branch\n- Year\n- College\n- Skills\n- Projects\n- Experience\n- Certifications\n- Preferred location\n- Remote preference\n- Career interests\n\nDo not ask the user to enter information that already exists in their profile.\n\nIf important information is missing, clearly indicate:\n\n\"Profile information missing\"\n\nand allow the user to update it.\n\n==================================================\n4. TARGET ROLE REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nDetermine the important requirements for the target role.\n\nRequirements may come from:\n\n1. A selected real job opportunity\n2. A user-provided job description\n3. Verified role requirement data\n4. Gemini reasoning based on the role\n\nPrioritize actual job requirements whenever available.\n\nSeparate requirements into:\n\n- Required skills\n- Preferred skills\n- Tools/technologies\n- Education\n- Experience\n- Projects\n- Certifications\n- Soft skills\n\nDo not claim that every job requires the same skills.\n\n==================================================\n5. SKILL GAP ANALYSIS\n==================================================\n\nCompare:\n\nStudent Current Skills\n\nagainst\n\nTarget Role Requirements.\n\nClassify each requirement as:\n\nMATCHED\nPARTIALLY_MATCHED\nMISSING\nUNKNOWN\n\nExample:\n\nPython\nMATCHED\n\nMachine Learning\nMATCHED\n\nTensorFlow\nPARTIALLY_MATCHED\n\nDocker\nMISSING\n\nAWS\nMISSING\n\nDo not assume a skill is present unless supported by the user\'s profile, resume, project data, or verified information.\n\n==================================================\n6. SKILL GAP PRIORITY\n==================================================\n\nPrioritize gaps.\n\nUse:\n\nHIGH\nMEDIUM\nLOW\n\nHIGH:\nImportant requirement that is currently missing.\n\nMEDIUM:\nUseful requirement or partially matched skill.\n\nLOW:\nNice-to-have skill that should not delay applying.\n\nDo not overwhelm the student with 20\342\200\22330 skills.\n\nShow the most important gaps first.\n\nRecommended:\n\nTop 3\342\200\2236 priority gaps.\n\n==================================================\n7. CAREER READINESS SCORE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a transparent readiness score from 0\342\200\223100.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to arbitrarily generate the final score.\n\nUse a deterministic scoring function.\n\nSuggested approach:\n\nRequired skills: 40%\nPreferred skills: 15%\nProjects/experience: 20%\nTools/technologies: 10%\nEducation/certifications: 5%\nProfile completeness: 10%\n\nNormalize the result to 100.\n\nClearly explain:\n\n\"This is an estimated readiness score based on the available profile and target-role requirements. It is not a guarantee of job selection.\"\n\nIf actual job-specific requirements are available, prioritize them.\n\n==================================================\n8. PERSONALIZED CAREER PATH\n==================================================\n\nGenerate a path specifically for the user.\n\nExample:\n\nTARGET:\nMachine Learning Engineer Intern\n\nCURRENT READINESS:\n58%\n\nPATH:\n\nPHASE 1\nStrengthen ML fundamentals\nDuration: 1\342\200\2232 weeks\n\nPHASE 2\nLearn TensorFlow\nDuration: 1\342\200\2232 weeks\n\nPHASE 3\nLearn Docker and model deployment\nDuration: 1 week\n\nPHASE 4\nBuild an ML deployment project\nDuration: 2 weeks\n\nPHASE 5\nOptimize resume and ATS\nDuration: 2\342\200\2233 days\n\nPHASE 6\nRecheck job readiness\nDuration: 1 day\n\nDo not generate arbitrary durations without explaining that they are estimates.\n\n==================================================\n9. EACH CAREER PATH STEP\n==================================================\n\nEvery step should contain:\n\n- Title\n- Why it matters\n- Skills to learn\n- Estimated duration\n- Learning resources\n- Practice task\n- Recommended project\n- Completion criteria\n\nExample:\n\nSTEP:\nLearn Docker\n\nWHY:\nThe target role frequently requests containerization.\n\nLEARN:\n- Images\n- Containers\n- Dockerfile\n- Ports\n- Environment variables\n\nPRACTICE:\nContainerize an existing ML API.\n\nCOMPLETION:\nSuccessfully run the API inside Docker.\n\n==================================================\n10. LEARNING RESOURCES\n==================================================\n\nThis is important.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to invent fake URLs.\n\nPrefer resources from trusted sources such as:\n\n- Official documentation\n- Official tutorials\n- Government/education resources\n- Reputable educational platforms\n- Trusted university resources\n- High-quality GitHub repositories\n\nWhen possible, provide:\n\n- Resource title\n- Provider\n- Resource type\n- URL\n- Skill covered\n\nClearly distinguish verified resources from AI-generated suggestions.\n\nIf the system cannot verify a URL, do not present it as a verified resource.\n\n==================================================\n11. PROJECT RECOMMENDATIONS\n==================================================\n\nFor important skill gaps, recommend practical projects.\n\nProjects should be:\n\n- Beginner/intermediate appropriate\n- Relevant to the target role\n- Portfolio-worthy\n- Buildable by a student\n\nExample:\n\nMissing:\nML deployment\n\nRecommended project:\n\n\"Deploy a sentiment analysis model as a REST API using FastAPI and Docker.\"\n\nInclude:\n\n- Project objective\n- Technologies\n- Difficulty\n- Expected output\n- Skills demonstrated\n\nDo not recommend unnecessarily complex projects.\n\n==================================================\n12. ATS INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate with the existing ATS Scanner.\n\nIf the user has already scanned a resume:\n\nUse the ATS findings as additional evidence.\n\nExample:\n\nATS identifies:\n\n- Weak ML project descriptions\n- Missing TensorFlow keyword\n- Missing deployment experience\n\nCareer Path should incorporate these findings.\n\nExample:\n\n\"Improve your ML project description\"\n\nshould become a career-path task.\n\nProvide a CTA:\n\n\"Optimize Resume\"\n\nwhich opens the existing ATS feature where appropriate.\n\nDo NOT duplicate the ATS implementation.\n\nReuse the existing ATS system.\n\n==================================================\n13. OPPORTUNITIES INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate with the existing Opportunities section.\n\nIf a user selects:\n\n\"Prepare me for this opportunity\"\n\nNovaPath should:\n\n1. Retrieve opportunity requirements\n2. Retrieve student profile\n3. Compare them\n4. Identify gaps\n5. Create personalized path\n6. Recommend resources\n7. Recommend projects\n8. Estimate readiness\n9. Tell the user what to improve before applying\n\nAdd a CTA:\n\n\"Build My Path to This Role\"\n\n==================================================\n14. AGENT NOVA INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nThe Career Path feature should be usable by Agent Nova.\n\nFor example:\n\nUser:\n\n\"I want to become an ML Engineer and get an internship in the next four months.\"\n\nAgent Nova should be able to:\n\n1. Understand the goal\n2. Retrieve profile\n3. Retrieve memory\n4. Identify target role\n5. Analyze current skills\n6. Identify gaps\n7. Generate career path\n8. Recommend resources\n9. Recommend projects\n10. Create milestones\n11. Track progress\n\nThis should be represented as a genuine multi-step workflow.\n\nDo NOT implement this as a fake list of steps that only appears visually.\n\nThe backend should actually execute the required operations.\n\n==================================================\n15. MEMORY INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing Memory Bank when relevant.\n\nExamples:\n\nIf the user previously said:\n\n\"I prefer remote internships.\"\n\nThe Career Path should consider that preference when suggesting opportunities.\n\nIf the user completed:\n\n\"Python fundamentals\"\n\nthe Career Path should not repeatedly recommend beginner Python resources.\n\nIf the user has already completed a project:\n\nUse that information to avoid unnecessary repetition.\n\nDo not expose unrelated private memory.\n\n==================================================\n16. PROGRESS TRACKING\n==================================================\n\nAllow users to mark milestones:\n\nNot Started\nIn Progress\nCompleted\n\nExample:\n\nPython\n\342\234\223 Completed\n\nTensorFlow\n\342\227\217 In Progress\n\nDocker\n\342\227\213 Not Started\n\nProject\n\342\227\213 Not Started\n\nStore progress in Firestore.\n\n==================================================\n17. FIRESTORE\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing Firebase/Firestore integration.\n\nDo not create a separate database.\n\nSuggested structure:\n\nusers/{userId}/careerPaths/{careerPathId}\n\nExample:\n\n{\n  careerPathId,\n  targetRole,\n  targetOpportunityId,\n  readinessScore,\n  createdAt,\n  updatedAt,\n  status,\n  skillGaps: [],\n  phases: [],\n  milestones: [],\n  resources: [],\n  projects: []\n}\n\nProgress can be stored inside the career path document or using an appropriate subcollection depending on the existing project architecture.\n\nFollow the current NovaPath Firestore conventions.\n\n==================================================\n18. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nA user must only access their own career paths.\n\nDo not use:\n\nallow read, write: if true;\n\nUse authenticated user ownership.\n\nDo not expose sensitive profile information.\n\nDo not expose Gemini API credentials.\n\n==================================================\n19. GEMINI\n==================================================\n\nReuse the EXISTING Gemini integration.\n\nDo NOT create another API key.\n\nDo NOT create another Gemini client.\n\nDo NOT expose GEMINI_API_KEY to the frontend.\n\nUse the existing server-side Gemini service.\n\nGemini should be responsible for:\n\n- Semantic analysis\n- Requirement interpretation\n- Skill-gap reasoning\n- Personalized recommendations\n- Learning-path generation\n- Project recommendations\n\nThe application should be responsible for:\n\n- Final readiness calculation\n- Data validation\n- Progress tracking\n- User authorization\n- Persistence\n\n==================================================\n20. AI OUTPUT VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nGemini must return structured JSON.\n\nValidate the response before storing it.\n\nIf Gemini returns invalid JSON:\n\nRetry safely or return a controlled error.\n\nNever allow malformed AI output to crash the application.\n\nNever invent user achievements.\n\nNever invent user skills.\n\nNever recommend that a student falsely claim a skill on a resume.\n\nUse language such as:\n\n\"Learn this skill if it is relevant to your target role.\"\n\n==================================================\n21. UI DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a polished dashboard.\n\nTop section:\n\nPERSONALIZED CAREER PATH\n\nTarget:\nMachine Learning Engineer\n\nReadiness:\n58/100\n\nEstimated preparation:\n8 weeks\n\nThen:\n\nYOUR SKILL GAPS\n\n\360\237\224\264 High Priority\n\360\237\237\240 Medium Priority\n\360\237\237\241 Low Priority\n\nThen:\n\nYOUR LEARNING PATH\n\nTimeline with phases.\n\nThen:\n\nLEARNING RESOURCES\n\nCards containing:\n\nResource\nProvider\nSkill\nType\nLink\n\nThen:\n\nRECOMMENDED PROJECTS\n\nThen:\n\nPROGRESS\n\nThen:\n\nNEXT ACTION\n\nExample:\n\n\"Complete TensorFlow fundamentals\"\n\nCTA:\n\n\"Start Learning\"\n\n==================================================\n22. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nIf the user has no career path:\n\nShow:\n\n\"Choose a target role to build your personalized career path.\"\n\nButton:\n\n\"Build My Career Path\"\n\n==================================================\n23. MOBILE RESPONSIVENESS\n==================================================\n\nThe page must work on:\n\nDesktop\nTablet\nMobile\n\nDo not sacrifice existing responsive behavior.\n\n==================================================\n24. ERROR HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nHandle:\n\n- Missing profile\n- Missing target role\n- Gemini failure\n- Invalid Gemini response\n- Firestore failure\n- Network failure\n- Missing opportunity requirements\n- Resource verification failure\n\nShow useful user-friendly messages.\n\nDo not expose technical stack traces to users.\n\n==================================================\n25. HACKATHON DEMO OPTIMIZATION\n==================================================\n\nThe feature must be optimized for a 3-minute demo.\n\nThe ideal demo should be:\n\n1. Select a real target opportunity\n2. Show student profile\n3. Click \"Build My Path\"\n4. Show readiness score\n5. Show 3 major skill gaps\n6. Show personalized learning path\n7. Show verified resources\n8. Show recommended project\n9. Mark one milestone complete\n10. Show updated progress\n\nThe experience should feel fast.\n\nCache or reuse previously generated results where appropriate.\n\n==================================================\n26. DO NOT OVERBUILD\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT implement:\n\n- Full learning management system\n- Video hosting\n- Course marketplace\n- Social networking\n- Complex recommendation ML model\n- Cryptocurrency\n- Blockchain\n- Microservices\n- Separate database\n- Custom model training\n\nKeep the implementation hackathon-friendly.\n\n==================================================\n27. BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementing the feature, verify that these still work:\n\n- Login\n- Agent Hub\n- Agent Nova\n- AI Coach\n- ATS Scanner\n- Profile & Skills\n- Opportunities\n- Memory Bank\n- Firebase Authentication\n- Firestore\n- Firebase Storage\n- Existing Gemini features\n\nDo not modify unrelated functionality.\n\n==================================================\n28. FINAL IMPLEMENTATION REPORT\n==================================================\n\nAfter completing the implementation, report:\n\n1. Files created\n2. Files modified\n3. Components created\n4. API routes created/modified\n5. Firestore collections/documents used\n6. Gemini functions created/modified\n7. Environment variables required\n8. Security changes\n9. Dependencies added\n10. Tests performed\n11. Known limitations\n12. Manual Firebase configuration required\n13. Any remaining work\n\nDo not reveal secret values.\n\nMost importantly:\n\nFIRST inspect the existing codebase.\n\nTHEN implement the feature.\n\nDo not rewrite working NovaPath features unnecessarily."
    items {
      text: "I want to add a new major feature to my existing NovaPath application called:\n\nPERSONALIZED CAREER PATH\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is an EXISTING application.\n\nDo NOT rebuild the application from scratch.\n\nDo NOT replace the current UI design.\n\nDo NOT remove or break any existing functionality.\n\nPreserve all existing features, including:\n\n- Agent Hub\n- Agent Nova\n- AI Coach\n- ATS Scanner\n- Profile & Skills\n- Opportunities\n- Memory Bank\n- Firebase Authentication\n- Firebase Firestore\n- Firebase Storage\n- Existing Gemini integration\n- Existing server-side Express architecture\n- Existing API routes\n- Existing navigation and design system\n\nFirst inspect the existing codebase and understand how these features are currently implemented.\n\nThen implement the Career Path feature using the existing architecture and reusable components wherever possible.\n\n==================================================\nPRODUCT PURPOSE\n==================================================\n\nNovaPath is an AI career execution platform for students.\n\nThe new Career Path feature should answer:\n\n\"If I want to get this particular job, but I am not currently qualified, what exactly should I learn, build, and improve to become ready for that role?\"\n\nThe feature must NOT simply generate a generic career roadmap.\n\nIt must create a PERSONALIZED career path based on:\n\n- Student profile\n- Current skills\n- Education\n- Projects\n- Experience\n- Certifications\n- Target job\n- Target job requirements\n- Existing ATS analysis when available\n- Previously completed learning milestones\n- User preferences stored in memory when relevant\n\n==================================================\nCORE USER FLOW\n==================================================\n\nImplement this flow:\n\nStudent\n \342\206\223\nSelect Target Career / Job\n \342\206\223\nLoad Student Profile\n \342\206\223\nAnalyze Target Role Requirements\n \342\206\223\nCompare Student Skills vs Requirements\n \342\206\223\nIdentify Skill Gaps\n \342\206\223\nPrioritize Skill Gaps\n \342\206\223\nGenerate Personalized Career Path\n \342\206\223\nRecommend Verified Learning Resources\n \342\206\223\nRecommend Practical Projects\n \342\206\223\nCreate Timeline\n \342\206\223\nTrack Progress\n \342\206\223\nRecalculate Career Readiness\n \342\206\223\nRecommend When To Apply\n\n==================================================\n1. NEW NAVIGATION SECTION\n==================================================\n\nAdd:\n\nCareer Path\n\nto the existing navigation.\n\nUse the existing NovaPath visual language.\n\nDo not redesign the entire navbar.\n\nThe new page should feel like a native part of NovaPath.\n\nSuggested page title:\n\n\"Personalized Career Path\"\n\nSubtitle:\n\n\"Your step-by-step path from where you are today to the role you want.\"\n\n==================================================\n2. CAREER TARGET SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nAllow the student to select or enter a target role.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Machine Learning Engineer\n- Data Scientist\n- AI Engineer\n- Data Analyst\n- Full Stack Developer\n- Backend Developer\n- Software Engineer\n- Cloud Engineer\n\nAlso allow:\n\n\"Use an opportunity from Opportunities\"\n\nIf the user selects an actual job opportunity, use that opportunity\'s requirements instead of generating generic requirements.\n\n==================================================\n3. STUDENT PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nRetrieve the authenticated user\'s existing profile.\n\nUse available information such as:\n\n- Name\n- Degree\n- Branch\n- Year\n- College\n- Skills\n- Projects\n- Experience\n- Certifications\n- Preferred location\n- Remote preference\n- Career interests\n\nDo not ask the user to enter information that already exists in their profile.\n\nIf important information is missing, clearly indicate:\n\n\"Profile information missing\"\n\nand allow the user to update it.\n\n==================================================\n4. TARGET ROLE REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nDetermine the important requirements for the target role.\n\nRequirements may come from:\n\n1. A selected real job opportunity\n2. A user-provided job description\n3. Verified role requirement data\n4. Gemini reasoning based on the role\n\nPrioritize actual job requirements whenever available.\n\nSeparate requirements into:\n\n- Required skills\n- Preferred skills\n- Tools/technologies\n- Education\n- Experience\n- Projects\n- Certifications\n- Soft skills\n\nDo not claim that every job requires the same skills.\n\n==================================================\n5. SKILL GAP ANALYSIS\n==================================================\n\nCompare:\n\nStudent Current Skills\n\nagainst\n\nTarget Role Requirements.\n\nClassify each requirement as:\n\nMATCHED\nPARTIALLY_MATCHED\nMISSING\nUNKNOWN\n\nExample:\n\nPython\nMATCHED\n\nMachine Learning\nMATCHED\n\nTensorFlow\nPARTIALLY_MATCHED\n\nDocker\nMISSING\n\nAWS\nMISSING\n\nDo not assume a skill is present unless supported by the user\'s profile, resume, project data, or verified information.\n\n==================================================\n6. SKILL GAP PRIORITY\n==================================================\n\nPrioritize gaps.\n\nUse:\n\nHIGH\nMEDIUM\nLOW\n\nHIGH:\nImportant requirement that is currently missing.\n\nMEDIUM:\nUseful requirement or partially matched skill.\n\nLOW:\nNice-to-have skill that should not delay applying.\n\nDo not overwhelm the student with 20\342\200\22330 skills.\n\nShow the most important gaps first.\n\nRecommended:\n\nTop 3\342\200\2236 priority gaps.\n\n==================================================\n7. CAREER READINESS SCORE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a transparent readiness score from 0\342\200\223100.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to arbitrarily generate the final score.\n\nUse a deterministic scoring function.\n\nSuggested approach:\n\nRequired skills: 40%\nPreferred skills: 15%\nProjects/experience: 20%\nTools/technologies: 10%\nEducation/certifications: 5%\nProfile completeness: 10%\n\nNormalize the result to 100.\n\nClearly explain:\n\n\"This is an estimated readiness score based on the available profile and target-role requirements. It is not a guarantee of job selection.\"\n\nIf actual job-specific requirements are available, prioritize them.\n\n==================================================\n8. PERSONALIZED CAREER PATH\n==================================================\n\nGenerate a path specifically for the user.\n\nExample:\n\nTARGET:\nMachine Learning Engineer Intern\n\nCURRENT READINESS:\n58%\n\nPATH:\n\nPHASE 1\nStrengthen ML fundamentals\nDuration: 1\342\200\2232 weeks\n\nPHASE 2\nLearn TensorFlow\nDuration: 1\342\200\2232 weeks\n\nPHASE 3\nLearn Docker and model deployment\nDuration: 1 week\n\nPHASE 4\nBuild an ML deployment project\nDuration: 2 weeks\n\nPHASE 5\nOptimize resume and ATS\nDuration: 2\342\200\2233 days\n\nPHASE 6\nRecheck job readiness\nDuration: 1 day\n\nDo not generate arbitrary durations without explaining that they are estimates.\n\n==================================================\n9. EACH CAREER PATH STEP\n==================================================\n\nEvery step should contain:\n\n- Title\n- Why it matters\n- Skills to learn\n- Estimated duration\n- Learning resources\n- Practice task\n- Recommended project\n- Completion criteria\n\nExample:\n\nSTEP:\nLearn Docker\n\nWHY:\nThe target role frequently requests containerization.\n\nLEARN:\n- Images\n- Containers\n- Dockerfile\n- Ports\n- Environment variables\n\nPRACTICE:\nContainerize an existing ML API.\n\nCOMPLETION:\nSuccessfully run the API inside Docker.\n\n==================================================\n10. LEARNING RESOURCES\n==================================================\n\nThis is important.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to invent fake URLs.\n\nPrefer resources from trusted sources such as:\n\n- Official documentation\n- Official tutorials\n- Government/education resources\n- Reputable educational platforms\n- Trusted university resources\n- High-quality GitHub repositories\n\nWhen possible, provide:\n\n- Resource title\n- Provider\n- Resource type\n- URL\n- Skill covered\n\nClearly distinguish verified resources from AI-generated suggestions.\n\nIf the system cannot verify a URL, do not present it as a verified resource.\n\n==================================================\n11. PROJECT RECOMMENDATIONS\n==================================================\n\nFor important skill gaps, recommend practical projects.\n\nProjects should be:\n\n- Beginner/intermediate appropriate\n- Relevant to the target role\n- Portfolio-worthy\n- Buildable by a student\n\nExample:\n\nMissing:\nML deployment\n\nRecommended project:\n\n\"Deploy a sentiment analysis model as a REST API using FastAPI and Docker.\"\n\nInclude:\n\n- Project objective\n- Technologies\n- Difficulty\n- Expected output\n- Skills demonstrated\n\nDo not recommend unnecessarily complex projects.\n\n==================================================\n12. ATS INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate with the existing ATS Scanner.\n\nIf the user has already scanned a resume:\n\nUse the ATS findings as additional evidence.\n\nExample:\n\nATS identifies:\n\n- Weak ML project descriptions\n- Missing TensorFlow keyword\n- Missing deployment experience\n\nCareer Path should incorporate these findings.\n\nExample:\n\n\"Improve your ML project description\"\n\nshould become a career-path task.\n\nProvide a CTA:\n\n\"Optimize Resume\"\n\nwhich opens the existing ATS feature where appropriate.\n\nDo NOT duplicate the ATS implementation.\n\nReuse the existing ATS system.\n\n==================================================\n13. OPPORTUNITIES INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate with the existing Opportunities section.\n\nIf a user selects:\n\n\"Prepare me for this opportunity\"\n\nNovaPath should:\n\n1. Retrieve opportunity requirements\n2. Retrieve student profile\n3. Compare them\n4. Identify gaps\n5. Create personalized path\n6. Recommend resources\n7. Recommend projects\n8. Estimate readiness\n9. Tell the user what to improve before applying\n\nAdd a CTA:\n\n\"Build My Path to This Role\"\n\n==================================================\n14. AGENT NOVA INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nThe Career Path feature should be usable by Agent Nova.\n\nFor example:\n\nUser:\n\n\"I want to become an ML Engineer and get an internship in the next four months.\"\n\nAgent Nova should be able to:\n\n1. Understand the goal\n2. Retrieve profile\n3. Retrieve memory\n4. Identify target role\n5. Analyze current skills\n6. Identify gaps\n7. Generate career path\n8. Recommend resources\n9. Recommend projects\n10. Create milestones\n11. Track progress\n\nThis should be represented as a genuine multi-step workflow.\n\nDo NOT implement this as a fake list of steps that only appears visually.\n\nThe backend should actually execute the required operations.\n\n==================================================\n15. MEMORY INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing Memory Bank when relevant.\n\nExamples:\n\nIf the user previously said:\n\n\"I prefer remote internships.\"\n\nThe Career Path should consider that preference when suggesting opportunities.\n\nIf the user completed:\n\n\"Python fundamentals\"\n\nthe Career Path should not repeatedly recommend beginner Python resources.\n\nIf the user has already completed a project:\n\nUse that information to avoid unnecessary repetition.\n\nDo not expose unrelated private memory.\n\n==================================================\n16. PROGRESS TRACKING\n==================================================\n\nAllow users to mark milestones:\n\nNot Started\nIn Progress\nCompleted\n\nExample:\n\nPython\n\342\234\223 Completed\n\nTensorFlow\n\342\227\217 In Progress\n\nDocker\n\342\227\213 Not Started\n\nProject\n\342\227\213 Not Started\n\nStore progress in Firestore.\n\n==================================================\n17. FIRESTORE\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing Firebase/Firestore integration.\n\nDo not create a separate database.\n\nSuggested structure:\n\nusers/{userId}/careerPaths/{careerPathId}\n\nExample:\n\n{\n  careerPathId,\n  targetRole,\n  targetOpportunityId,\n  readinessScore,\n  createdAt,\n  updatedAt,\n  status,\n  skillGaps: [],\n  phases: [],\n  milestones: [],\n  resources: [],\n  projects: []\n}\n\nProgress can be stored inside the career path document or using an appropriate subcollection depending on the existing project architecture.\n\nFollow the current NovaPath Firestore conventions.\n\n==================================================\n18. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nA user must only access their own career paths.\n\nDo not use:\n\nallow read, write: if true;\n\nUse authenticated user ownership.\n\nDo not expose sensitive profile information.\n\nDo not expose Gemini API credentials.\n\n==================================================\n19. GEMINI\n==================================================\n\nReuse the EXISTING Gemini integration.\n\nDo NOT create another API key.\n\nDo NOT create another Gemini client.\n\nDo NOT expose GEMINI_API_KEY to the frontend.\n\nUse the existing server-side Gemini service.\n\nGemini should be responsible for:\n\n- Semantic analysis\n- Requirement interpretation\n- Skill-gap reasoning\n- Personalized recommendations\n- Learning-path generation\n- Project recommendations\n\nThe application should be responsible for:\n\n- Final readiness calculation\n- Data validation\n- Progress tracking\n- User authorization\n- Persistence\n\n==================================================\n20. AI OUTPUT VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nGemini must return structured JSON.\n\nValidate the response before storing it.\n\nIf Gemini returns invalid JSON:\n\nRetry safely or return a controlled error.\n\nNever allow malformed AI output to crash the application.\n\nNever invent user achievements.\n\nNever invent user skills.\n\nNever recommend that a student falsely claim a skill on a resume.\n\nUse language such as:\n\n\"Learn this skill if it is relevant to your target role.\"\n\n==================================================\n21. UI DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a polished dashboard.\n\nTop section:\n\nPERSONALIZED CAREER PATH\n\nTarget:\nMachine Learning Engineer\n\nReadiness:\n58/100\n\nEstimated preparation:\n8 weeks\n\nThen:\n\nYOUR SKILL GAPS\n\n\360\237\224\264 High Priority\n\360\237\237\240 Medium Priority\n\360\237\237\241 Low Priority\n\nThen:\n\nYOUR LEARNING PATH\n\nTimeline with phases.\n\nThen:\n\nLEARNING RESOURCES\n\nCards containing:\n\nResource\nProvider\nSkill\nType\nLink\n\nThen:\n\nRECOMMENDED PROJECTS\n\nThen:\n\nPROGRESS\n\nThen:\n\nNEXT ACTION\n\nExample:\n\n\"Complete TensorFlow fundamentals\"\n\nCTA:\n\n\"Start Learning\"\n\n==================================================\n22. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nIf the user has no career path:\n\nShow:\n\n\"Choose a target role to build your personalized career path.\"\n\nButton:\n\n\"Build My Career Path\"\n\n==================================================\n23. MOBILE RESPONSIVENESS\n==================================================\n\nThe page must work on:\n\nDesktop\nTablet\nMobile\n\nDo not sacrifice existing responsive behavior.\n\n==================================================\n24. ERROR HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nHandle:\n\n- Missing profile\n- Missing target role\n- Gemini failure\n- Invalid Gemini response\n- Firestore failure\n- Network failure\n- Missing opportunity requirements\n- Resource verification failure\n\nShow useful user-friendly messages.\n\nDo not expose technical stack traces to users.\n\n==================================================\n25. HACKATHON DEMO OPTIMIZATION\n==================================================\n\nThe feature must be optimized for a 3-minute demo.\n\nThe ideal demo should be:\n\n1. Select a real target opportunity\n2. Show student profile\n3. Click \"Build My Path\"\n4. Show readiness score\n5. Show 3 major skill gaps\n6. Show personalized learning path\n7. Show verified resources\n8. Show recommended project\n9. Mark one milestone complete\n10. Show updated progress\n\nThe experience should feel fast.\n\nCache or reuse previously generated results where appropriate.\n\n==================================================\n26. DO NOT OVERBUILD\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT implement:\n\n- Full learning management system\n- Video hosting\n- Course marketplace\n- Social networking\n- Complex recommendation ML model\n- Cryptocurrency\n- Blockchain\n- Microservices\n- Separate database\n- Custom model training\n\nKeep the implementation hackathon-friendly.\n\n==================================================\n27. BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementing the feature, verify that these still work:\n\n- Login\n- Agent Hub\n- Agent Nova\n- AI Coach\n- ATS Scanner\n- Profile & Skills\n- Opportunities\n- Memory Bank\n- Firebase Authentication\n- Firestore\n- Firebase Storage\n- Existing Gemini features\n\nDo not modify unrelated functionality.\n\n==================================================\n28. FINAL IMPLEMENTATION REPORT\n==================================================\n\nAfter completing the implementation, report:\n\n1. Files created\n2. Files modified\n3. Components created\n4. API routes created/modified\n5. Firestore collections/documents used\n6. Gemini functions created/modified\n7. Environment variables required\n8. Security changes\n9. Dependencies added\n10. Tests performed\n11. Known limitations\n12. Manual Firebase configuration required\n13. Any remaining work\n\nDo not reveal secret values.\n\nMost importantly:\n\nFIRST inspect the existing codebase.\n\nTHEN implement the feature.\n\nDo not rewrite working NovaPath features unnecessarily."
    }
  }
}
