      nanos: 345728446
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the data structures needed for the \"Personalized Career Path\" feature. Specifically, I\'ve started listing the required data types, starting with the `CareerPath` structure. I\'m considering its key attributes, such as `id`, `careerPathId`, `userId`, and `target`. I will be going over what data fields will be in the `target` field.\n\n\n**Analyzing Target Details**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the `target` field of the `CareerPath` structure. The attributes I\'ve landed on include `targetOpportunityId`, `targetJobDescription`, `readinessScore`, `estimatedWeeks`, `status`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and more. I am thinking of including details such as `skillGaps`, `phases`, `resources`, and `projects`, and the `atsInsights`. I am also considering including a `nextAction`.\n\n\n**Defining Career Steps**\n\nI\'m now focusing on detailing the `phases` within the career path, specifically defining the `CareerPhase` structure. It will include attributes like `id`, `phaseNumber`, `title`, `duration`, `focus`, and a list of `CareerStep` objects. These steps will have their own structures, too, including details about skills, resources, and tasks. I am working through the data requirements for each of these steps, including resources.\n\n\n**Elaborating Project Details**\n\nI\'ve just defined the `CareerProject` structure, including attributes like `id`, `title`, and `technologies`. I\'m also including `objective`, `difficulty`, and expected output, to flesh out the detail on the individual project. The new attributes are `skillsDemonstrated`, `milestoneStepId`, and `status`.\n\nI\'m also looking into a `CareerScoreBreakdown` structure, which will capture a more detailed scoring system including weights for Required and Preferred Skills, Projects, Tools, Education, and profile completeness. The final `total` score and `calculationExplanation` are included as well. I\'ll need to define how the scoring weights work and how they impact the total.\n\n\n**Verifying Resources**\n\nI\'m now focusing on resource verification. I need to make sure Gemini doesn\'t generate fake URLs. I\'m prioritizing official documentation, tutorials, and reputable educational platforms. My goal is to curate a catalog of verified, high-quality resources, clearly distinguishing verified sources from AI-generated suggestions.\n\n\n**Integrating ATS Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating ATS data into the career path feature. I\'m focusing on retrieving user\'s previous ATS reports and checking them for content improvements like including missing keywords and quantifying bullet points. These findings are then automatically incorporated into the career path or presented as a call-to-action to optimize the resume. I\'m also adding a call-to-action to the ATS Scanner tab to optimize the resume. I\'m also working on integrating Opportunities data.\n\n\n**Implementing Career Path Triggers**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Career Path feature with the Nova agent. The goal is that when a user expresses a target career like \"ML Engineer,\" Nova can trigger or recommend opening a relevant Career Path automatically.\n\nI\'m also working on Memory Bank integration. I\'ll be retrieving the user\'s saved memories, like preferences and completed courses, during Career Path generation. This will allow the system to skip introductory steps for skills the user has already mastered. I\'m excited about how personalization this will bring.\n\nFinally, I\'m working through the Firestore integration, updating the `firestore.rules` and `firebase-blueprint.json` files and creating the `careerPathService.ts` for data operations, which will include error handling. I\'m also planning the server-side Gemini endpoints for generating paths, which will include student profiles, target roles, ATS reports, and memories to determine skill gaps and relevant phases, tasks, and portfolio suggestions.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 541229447
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
